.TH UNIM-SETTINGS 1 "August 2026" "UNIM 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unim\-settings \- UNIM settings app and first\-run wizard (Slint)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unim\-settings
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBunim\-settings\fR is the cross\-platform settings application for UNIM
(Universal Next\-generation Input Method), built with Slint (winit + Skia)
from a single codebase shared with the Windows build. It edits the same
configuration file the daemon reads (\fI~/.config/unim/config.yaml\fR), with
every change synced live to the running daemon over D\-Bus, and it hosts the
first\-run installation wizard.
.PP
On Linux the GTK4 + libadwaita settings dialog is a separate binary,
\fBunim\-settings\-gtk\fR(1); the two edit the same configuration and may
coexist. System launchers (tray indicator, GNOME extension) currently open
the GTK dialog, so this Slint entry is installed with \fBNoDisplay=true\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-first\-run
Launch the full first\-run wizard unconditionally (WELCOME, LICENSE,
default\-IME, TypeFix, FINISH). Use this to re\-run the wizard by hand at
any time, even after it has already been completed once.
.TP
.B \-\-first\-run\-if\-needed
Autostart\-only gate. If the wizard has already been completed (its
seen\-version file exists), exit immediately and silently with status 0 —
no window, no singleton lock, no notification. Otherwise behaves like
\fB\-\-first\-run\fR. This flag is used by the per\-login autostart entry
\fIio.github.from104.unim.FirstRun.desktop\fR and is not meant to be run
manually.
.TP
.B \-\-whats\-new
Show only the pages introduced since the last completed version — an
update\-notes channel for package upgrades.
.SH DEFAULT INPUT METHOD
On the default\-IME page the wizard sets UNIM as the default input method
in\-process via \fBim\-config \-n unim\fR(8). The change is written to
\fI~/.xinputrc\fR and takes effect from the next login. If \fBim\-config\fR is
not installed, the wizard writes \fBrun_im unim\fR to \fI~/.xinputrc\fR
directly (same format im\-config uses).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/unim/config.yaml
User configuration file (single source of truth).
.TP
.B ~/.local/state/unim/wizard\-seen\-version
Records the version at which the wizard was last completed; the
\fB\-\-first\-run\-if\-needed\fR gate reads it to decide whether to stay silent.
.TP
.B /etc/xdg/autostart/io.github.from104.unim.FirstRun.desktop
Per\-login autostart entry that runs \fBunim\-settings \-\-first\-run\-if\-needed\fR.
.TP
.B ~/.xinputrc
Input\-method selection written by \fBim\-config\fR (or the wizard fallback).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unim (1),
.BR unim\-settings\-gtk (1),
.BR unim\-daemon (1),
.BR unim\-cli (1),
.BR im\-config (8)
